WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.066
Reimagining Public Financial Management in
India.

00:00:05.116 --> 00:00:05.822
Part one:

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.670
the executive summary.

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.959
Governments create and maintain public
goods, deliver public services,

00:00:14.009 --> 00:00:15.807
and provide social welfare.

00:00:15.857 --> 00:00:18.612
To do this they need financial resources:

00:00:18.662 --> 00:00:23.812
revenues from taxes and fees, income from
government-owned entities, grants,

00:00:23.862 --> 00:00:24.770
and borrowing.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.720
Public financial management, or PFM, is
how governments manage public resources,

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.695
both revenue and expenditure,

00:00:33.745 --> 00:00:37.986
and the impact those resources have on the
economy and society.

00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:42.278
It is about process, how governments
manage, and about results.

00:00:43.828 --> 00:00:49.168
Governments in India and around the world
have adopted digital ways of working.

00:00:49.218 --> 00:00:54.081
Yet visibility into fiscal status, the
stocks and flows of public funds,

00:00:54.131 --> 00:00:55.445
remains a challenge.

00:00:55.495 --> 00:00:57.970
That uncertainty reaches vendors too.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.108
It raises transaction costs and risk
premiums,

00:01:01.158 --> 00:01:06.498
and it means people across the PFM landscape
lack key information at the moment

00:01:06.548 --> 00:01:07.658
they have to act.

00:01:09.208 --> 00:01:12.109
Why do these gaps persist after
digitisation?

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:14.930
Because of the number of entities
involved,

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:17.750
across every tier of the federal
hierarchy,

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:22.013
and the lack of standardisation in how
their systems manage data.

00:01:22.063 --> 00:01:26.998
Every new application creates the need for
more point-to-point integrations,

00:01:27.048 --> 00:01:29.425
a complicated and expensive exercise.

00:01:29.475 --> 00:01:34.934
Without interoperability, consistent and comprehensive
visibility is hard to ensure.

00:01:36.484 --> 00:01:41.675
Recent reforms, such as the Single Nodal
Agency model, have brought real progress:

00:01:41.725 --> 00:01:47.043
far better visibility into the status of funds
allotted to centrally funded schemes.

00:01:47.093 --> 00:01:49.728
But that visibility stops at the treasury.

00:01:49.778 --> 00:01:51.389
Once money has been spent,

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:56.311
there is limited information on the
outputs and outcomes of that expenditure,

00:01:56.361 --> 00:01:59.570
and the reporting on it suffers from the
same gaps.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.611
This paper reduces all of these challenges
to a single pivotal problem:

00:02:05.661 --> 00:02:10.792
the fragmented nature of information flows,
between government financial systems,

00:02:10.842 --> 00:02:13.670
and across financial and operational
systems.

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.871
The proposed answer has two parts.

00:02:17.921 --> 00:02:24.384
First, standardised fiscal and service events
that cover the entire PFM lifecycle:

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:27.164
nine fiscal events in three groups.

00:02:27.214 --> 00:02:29.388
Plan, estimate and sanction.

00:02:29.438 --> 00:02:31.533
Demand, receipt and credit.

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:33.439
Bill, payment and debit.

00:02:33.489 --> 00:02:39.873
Second, a data exchange platform, the India
Financial Information Exchange, iFIX,

00:02:39.923 --> 00:02:43.130
which puts that interoperability to work.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.655
Together, they give real-time visibility
into the status and flow of funds.

00:02:49.705 --> 00:02:54.680
They allow planning, budgeting and
forecasting on complete and timely data;

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.824
structured revenue mobilisation;

00:02:56.874 --> 00:02:58.433
participatory budgeting;

00:02:58.483 --> 00:03:00.376
output and outcome reporting;

00:03:00.426 --> 00:03:01.984
even real-time auditing.

00:03:02.034 --> 00:03:06.071
And they lay the foundation for smart
contracts and reliable,

00:03:06.121 --> 00:03:09.086
timely payments to vendors and
beneficiaries.

00:03:11.086 --> 00:03:11.433
Next:

00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:15.644
how public financial management works in
India today.
